# NO REWRITES HERE. On Cloudflare Pages a matching _redirects rule is followed
# EVEN WHEN A STATIC FILE EXISTS AT THAT PATH ("Redirects are always followed,
# regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming request",
# developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/). Static files do NOT
# win, as they do on Netlify. Until 2026-10-08 this file had
#   /games/*     /  200
#   /category/*  /  200
# as a safety net for games published after the last portal build, and those two
# lines served the HOMEPAGE html for every prerendered game and category page
# (and for their index.pageContext.json files): crawlers and link previews only
# ever saw the homepage title and og:image.
#
# The safety net now lives in the top-level 404.html (scripts/postbuild-404.mjs):
# a /games/<slug> or /category/<name> URL with no static html gets that 404 page,
# whose inline script hands the URL to the app (/?spa=<path>) and the homepage's
# SPA-fallback effect (pages/index/+Page.tsx) client-routes to the real page.
# Every other unknown URL is a plain HTTP 404.
#
# A 200-rewrite whose target is "/index.html" is silently ignored by Pages (a
# rewrite to "/" works; verified 2026-10-06). Pages' single-page-app mode (every
# unknown URL -> 200 + homepage) only applies when there is NO top-level 404.html.
# Only add 301/302 redirects for URLs that have no static file of their own.
